{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And may Elohim be with you</b> in this counsel — he said to him: go, rule with might. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 18:19). And Rabbi Abraham explained: hear my voice, and may YHWH be your help to make you succeed through my counsel. But below (Exodus 18:23) he said, <b>If you do this thing, and Elohim commands you</b>, which means: if you do the thing and Elohim commands you to do it, then you will be able to stand firm, so that you may rule with might. And there is no doubt that he did so." "<b>And you shall be for the people opposite Elohim</b> — opposite Elohim. One should read: you, on their behalf, stand opposite Elohim to pray to Him, in the sense of \"In the night I cry out opposite You\" (Psalms 88:2)." "<b>And you shall bring the matters</b> that they seek <b>to Elohim</b> — he acknowledged to him concerning the first thing that he said: <b>for the people come to me to inquire of Elohim</b>. And it is possible that there was also counsel from him in this: he says, <b>you shall be for the people opposite Elohim</b> to sit in the Tent of Meeting, prepared before Him to inquire of Him, and this would not take the place of judgment."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "ר\"א refers to Rabbi Abraham Ibn Ezra."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:10:31.500584444Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}